                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I like this game because it brings me back to old RPGs.  I mean very old, like Commodore 64.  I like it because it's basic.  Why is it basic?\r\n1. To make a skill effective, you usually need to put points into it every time you gain a level.  This leads to your characters having only 1 skill that they always use in battle.  Be prepared to consider that skill use to be a \"basic attack\" and to repeatedly use that attack, every battle, for the whole game.\r\n2. The game is very grindy.  I enjoy grindy.  Not everyone does.\r\n3. The format gets repetitive, especially as you approach level 30 and as you try to climb to level 40.  Even as I enjoy the game, I have to take breaks because I get bored.\r\n\r\nI know this sounds like a negative review.  Again, this makes me nostalgic for very old RPGs.  It plays, sounds, and even looks like one.  Do not expect there to be many quality of life features.\r\n\r\nAlso, don't play this after playing Pen And Paper 2.  You will feel limited and the interface will feel clunky.",
